SU(2) power-TP2 exact compact-Bernstein certificate

commands:
  make -f Makefile.research prove_su2_power_tp2_compact_bernstein
  for m in 6 7 8 9 10 11; do
    ./prove_su2_power_tp2_compact_bernstein "$m" 0
    ./prove_su2_power_tp2_compact_bernstein "$m" 0 -1 wall
  done

compiler flags:
  g++ -O2 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion \
    -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror -pthread \
    prove_su2_power_tp2_compact_bernstein.cpp -lgmp \
    -o prove_su2_power_tp2_compact_bernstein

The worker count is selected at process start from the online processor
count, the one-minute machine load, and free RAM.  It is not fixed.
The following summaries were produced by a byte-identical copy of the
hash-bound binary while the machine was under load.

